{"step_index":93,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-12T15:17:15Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-12T18:17:15+03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-12T18:17:19+03:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-12T18:17:15+03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-12T18:17:19+03:00\nThe search for \"minio docker image pull access denied quay.io/minio/minio latest tag 2026\" returned the following summary:\nIf you are encountering an **\"access denied\"** or **\"unauthorized\"** error when trying to pull MinIO docker images from `minio/minio` (Docker Hub) or `quay.io/minio/minio`[1][2], it is because **MinIO has archived its open-source community edition and removed/restricted public anonymous access to its official container images**[3][4]. \n\nAdditionally, the `latest` tag or year-based tags (like `2026`) are generally not officially maintained release naming conventions for MinIO (which typically uses strict timestamp release tags like `RELEASE.YYYY-MM-DDTHH-MM-SSZ`).\n\nDepending on your use case, you have a few ways to resolve or work around this:\n\n### 1. Migrate to a Maintained Drop-In Fork (Recommended)\nBecause the original community project has been archived, continuing to rely on old, unpatched images presents security risks[5]. Several community-maintained forks of the open-source MinIO server exist as drop-in replacements that use the same environment variables, ports, and command-line arguments[5].\n\nFor example, **Silo** (`pgsty/silo`) is an actively maintained community fork of the MinIO server and console[5]:\n```yaml\nservices:\n  minio:\n    image: pgsty/silo:latest # or use a specific pinned release tag\n    environment:\n      MINIO_ROOT_USER: \"your-access-key\"\n      MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD: \"your-secret-key\"\n    ports:\n      - \"9000:9000\"\n      - \"9001:9001\"\n    command: server /data --console-address \":9001\"\n```\n\n### 2. Use Alternative S3-Compatible Object Storages\nIf you only need an S3-compatible API for local development, testing, or CI pipelines, consider swapping MinIO out for other lightweight S3 alternatives available on Docker Hub:\n* **LocalStack** (`localstack/localstack`) — Mock AWS services including S3.\n* **SeaweedFS** (`chrislusf/seaweedfs`) — A distributed storage system that includes an S3 API interface.\n* **Garage** (`dxflrs/garage`) — A lightweight S3-compatible storage service designed for self-hosting.\n\nSources:\n[1] [ibm.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEIsOBDBuFTY6IUH7bzAZoXVCfmMHwU5AkGJRoPzHNK6DKGJtpxSKSs8rrkBoYbvtxmAWpKd0wQBbjkUIadpcR4kJBgXGwYECKzr5X5pRQfFfMfUEciLwFqhE2G23acsZW2sMz9)\n[2] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF5rWwChzRYNUH5hmuOBrLKt2xmPKjP4vu0uAl15x7m4ImNtRel-fKyjQX8I3Q1a6F2LpGHwDeM1gpRrei7iYmNr1hP32rSi2wH3PPwBGFP8Cufjg982DuzeAfkvzodHiEO3QQtIo1xuhs=)\n[3] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE-W5dXSokZ9N1K5NsbKMRXGEA8svaQ2d4ZQ6Uu1nWo4EbbxSouqQyOV3qevWPJ9VLpBHs1odlWYxv82PDMcNXuDzH9bpSeeMJuHfIEbdnuA49r_cWTxG_9yMUQRmfDUSQd0b984lw=)\n[4] [stablebuild.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE0tIByEnFfc6_jFILbu0j6ErSVbY4cEs0bJuZwft-d_nzWkefURKfb02pMtxh03qmD-It5A2ybRkbl6ybdXsRmVaIrVAxk0_IMOelfiC6-vzt-Fc_laFH9otqRRvyvvJ06g-b2opOGpmnwwS2ozfhT7oGh6vss54liSKvoyVVS3mSVz50=)\n[5] [benwaraiotoko.dev](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHmZqApfi3qF6H84XLJaB2JUCG9oYNa-s2GmZfiy5xI0OrpAdSVg49rvD7SZKRud8Q_kRREPvJqNXt-FJSZmVT394WPSXiG89nLiQW1l-hJFfuk5JZIVq6hONxUKgsX0FgYahiUrwN58uokS9XZfwSQvit3Qg==)\n\nNote: Source URLs are HTTP redirects; check where they resolve if you need the direct link."}
